vibe-lang's patch for z3's timer (mizchi/vibe-lang#3883, scripts/z3_wasi/z3.patch, made for z3
4.15.8; src/util/scoped_timer.cpp is the same file in 4.16.0, so it applies unchanged).

z3's timer registers a handler with pthread_atfork, which stops the timer's threads in a forked
child. WASI has no fork, and the single-threaded libc of wasi-sdk 34 declares pthread_atfork but
defines it nowhere, so the executable doesn't link. On WASI the patch leaves the call out, and
pthread.h with it, which vibe-lang's toolchain didn't have. wasi-sdk 34 has pthread.h, so that
part changes nothing here. With the polling timer (Z3_POLLING_TIMER) the limit of try-for, which
every question of lengua's carries, starts no thread: z3 reads the clock as it works.

